      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-08T17:21:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on what Chris has done with DMSAA and consistency for ops that don\u0027t need it, RenderSteps are supposed to work visually the same whether or not they are in an msaa renderpass or not. This might mean that we need to tell the RenderStep whether or not stencil/depth/msaa are present for the renderpass when filling out its uniforms or vertices, but I think we can avoid that for now.\n\nThe RenderStep requiresStencil/MSAA are meant to be triggers so that if they are true for any recorded step in a DrawPass, then we\u0027d make sure the RenderPass was setup for stencil or msaa. The GraphicsPipeline then is set to match the RenderPassDesc, and we can assert that if the RenderStep needed stencil, etc. the RPDesc provides it. If the RS didn\u0027t need it, then the RPDesc can but doesn\u0027t have to provide it. We would just need to account for this combination during pre-compiling for the render steps that can be used in either mode.\n\n(NOTE: the fill-bounds step right now doesn\u0027t declare it requires msaa, but that\u0027s pedantic. Since it\u0027s always used with a stenciling step that does require msaa for the path curves, it would never need to be combined with a non-msaa RPDesc).",
      "parentUuid": "4e93c2ed_d0544106",
      "revId": "a77aa10889312e8df212c1fb7f455b19e1df282e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
